This project reimplements, in C#, protocol knowledge first worked out and measured on real hardware
by kbd-signal (https://github.com/Sora-bluesky/kbd-signal, MIT License, Copyright (c) sora
(Sora-bluesky)): the VIA raw HID lighting commands, the Keychron Q1 HE 8K's color and brightness
reset after an effect change and the dark-hold workaround for it, the brightness revert window, the
lossy VIA v3 brightness round trip, and verifying a custom channel with a speed round trip. No kbd-signal
source code is included.

The SetupAPI and HID declarations are adapted from OpenInzone
(https://github.com/penguinwokrs/openinzone, GPL-3.0, same author).

The Pulsar lighting protocols (Pulsar's own, and SayoDevice's as Pulsar's keyboards use it) are
reimplemented from the behaviour of Pulsar's web configurator, Bibimbap (https://bbb.pulsar.gg/), for
interoperability. No Pulsar or SayoDevice code is included.

